I get such a chill hearing Bob do that one.
听到鲍勃那样做，我感到一阵寒意。

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.629
He was such a secret weapon of the show.
他是这个节目的秘密武器。

00:13:16.629 --> 00:13:20.309
He was so good at being Future Ted telling his kids that story.
他很擅长成为未来的泰德，给他的孩子们讲这个故事。

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:26.629
And I think it's an underrated kind of like track in the overall song of our show.
我认为在我们节目的整体歌曲中，这是一首被低估的歌曲。

00:13:26.629 --> 00:13:30.230
You know, that was that's like a really crucial instrument in the orchestra there.
你知道，那是乐团中非常重要的乐器。

00:13:30.629 --> 00:13:31.533
And he was wonderful.
他很棒。

00:13:31.533 --> 00:13:32.437
It makes me miss him.
这让我想念他。

00:13:32.437 --> 00:13:33.469
He was just a great guy.
他只是一个很棒的人。

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.070
And he loved playing that part.
他喜欢扮演这个角色。

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.269
He took a lot of pride in being Future Ted.
他为成为未来的泰德感到非常自豪。

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:40.549
He and Josh developed a real bond because he's like, I'm future you.
他和乔什建立了真正的联系，因为他说，我就是未来​​的你。

00:13:40.549 --> 00:13:41.830
I'm the voice of future.
我是未来的声音。

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:43.950
And you guys like really became close over that.
你们真的因此变得很亲密。

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:44.709
And you hear it.
你听到了。

00:13:44.709 --> 00:13:45.990
He would watch the episode.
他会观看这一集。

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:50.350
he'd tap into where Ted was emotionally, and he'd perform that.
他会挖掘特德的情感，并做到这一点。

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.350
And I love that about him.
我喜欢他这一点。

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:53.490
And yeah, this is kind of the whole series in miniature.
是的，这是整个系列的缩影。

00:13:53.490 --> 00:14:02.190
Since this whole episode that you're having us on is a symposium on cold opens, this is another way we used cold opens, which is we liked teasing a mystery.
由于您让我们观看的这一整集是关于冷开的研讨会，这是我们使用冷开的另一种方式，我们喜欢戏弄一个谜。

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:09.549
We liked really getting right up to a mystery moment, hard-cutting the credits, and you have to stay tuned for the next 20 minutes to find out.
我们真的很喜欢直接进入一个神秘的时刻，严格剪辑制作人员名单，你必须在接下来的 20 分钟里继续关注才能找到答案。

00:14:09.549 --> 00:14:10.870
In this case, who's behind that umbrella?
那么，这把伞背后的人是谁呢？

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.990
It turns out to be Meryl Streep playing herself, you know.
你知道，原来是梅丽尔·斯特里普扮演她自己。

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.590
But you need to watch the rest of the episode.
但你需要观看该集的其余部分。

00:14:16.590 --> 00:14:26.509
And that is, that's what I mean by we usually, the cold open on how I met your mother was like a load bearing support of the architecture because we really start the story there.
也就是说，这就是我通常所说的，关于我如何遇见你母亲的冷开场就像建筑的承重支撑，因为我们真正从那里开始故事。

00:14:26.509 --> 00:14:28.990
We plant a mystery or we kick something off in some way.
我们埋下一个谜团，或者以某种方式拉开序幕。

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:32.669
We didn't do as many free standards as you guys did, which again are really hard to do.
我们没有像你们那样制定那么多免费标准，这又很难做到。

00:14:32.669 --> 00:14:47.250
One other thing I want to say about that cold open, again, you know, when Craig and I've been doing how we made your mother part of it is like the mystery of why people love the show so much why do people still want to talk about them and play them for their kids and all this stuff?
关于冷开场，我想说的另一件事是，你知道，当克雷格和我一直在做我们如何让你母亲参与其中时，就像一个谜：为什么人们如此喜欢这个节目，为什么人们仍然想谈论它们并为他们的孩子播放它们以及所有这些东西？

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:54.370
And one of the things that I think people find so much solace in is that it's a meaningful universe.
我认为人们能从中找到很多安慰的一件事是，这是一个有意义的宇宙。

00:14:54.370 --> 00:15:05.980
How I met your mother says the universe both in this show and presumably the one that you're existing in also is meaningful and every little encounter has meaning and it's kind of an antidote to cynicism.
《我是如何认识你母亲的》说，这部剧中的宇宙以及你所在的宇宙都是有意义的，每一次小小的相遇都有意义，它是愤世嫉俗的一剂解药。

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:21.289
It's an antidote to nihilism or chaos that there's a plan and there's benevolence and there's a guiding hand, and I think that even if people don't articulate it that way, that's part of the warmth they feel when they watch the show and why they keep coming back to it.
这是虚无主义或混乱的解药，有计划、有仁慈、有指导手，我认为即使人们不这样表达，这也是他们在观看节目时感受到的温暖的一部分，也是他们不断回归的原因。

00:15:21.289 --> 00:15:22.289
I so agree.
我非常同意。

00:15:22.289 --> 00:15:23.929
It's like comfort.
就像安慰一样。

00:15:23.929 --> 00:15:34.409
When I watch your show, it makes me feel like everything's okay in some way, and I want you guys to know, just yesterday, I met a woman who told me, she loves your podcast.
当我看你的节目时，这让我觉得在某种程度上一切都很好，我想让你们知道，就在昨天，我遇到了一个女人，她告诉我，她喜欢你的播客。

00:15:34.409 --> 00:15:35.649
She's an office ladies listener.
她是一名办公室女士听众。

