我会看一个。

00:34:36.015 --> 00:34:38.139
And this might surprise you, Jenna.
这可能会让你感到惊讶，珍娜。

00:34:38.139 --> 00:34:41.660
But I was feeling very nostalgic recently for beach games.
但最近我对沙滩游戏感到非常怀念。

00:34:41.660 --> 00:34:43.420
Oh, that doesn't surprise me.
哦，这并不令我惊讶。

00:34:43.420 --> 00:34:45.241
I mean, that was a hard shoot.
我的意思是，那是一次艰难的拍摄。

00:34:45.241 --> 00:34:47.851
Is that why you think it would surprise me?
这就是你认为这会让我感到惊讶的原因吗？

00:34:47.851 --> 00:34:49.854
Because it was a little grueling.
因为有点累。

00:34:49.854 --> 00:34:50.825
It was grueling.
这真是太折磨人了。

00:34:50.825 --> 00:34:52.525
We were outside in the heat.
我们在炎热的天气里。

00:34:52.525 --> 00:34:57.259
It was like dusty and sandy and like, like we got sunburned, it was long days.
尘土飞扬，沙尘滚滚，就像我们被晒伤一样，这是漫长的日子。

00:34:57.260 --> 00:35:01.659
But then at night it was freezing, but we had to be in our same clothes that we had.
但到了晚上，天气很冷，但我们必须穿着原来的衣服。

00:35:01.659 --> 00:35:03.139
That was the thing about beach games.
这就是沙滩游戏的特点。

00:35:03.139 --> 00:35:10.739
You established this warm weather clothing for the day, and then at night you were stuck with that same outfit and you were freezing.
你为白天准备了这套温暖的衣服，然后到了晚上你就穿着同样的衣服，然后你就冻僵了。

00:35:10.739 --> 00:35:11.780
And you were freezing, yeah.
而你却冻僵了，是的。

00:35:11.780 --> 00:35:22.480
So it was physically a difficult shoot, but you know, I was going through some old pictures and it was so just special in so many ways.
所以这在物理上是一次困难的拍摄，但你知道，我正在浏览一些旧照片，它在很多方面都很特别。

00:35:23.150 --> 00:35:27.710
Okay, one, I loved my storyline with letting Andy just float away.
好吧，第一，我喜欢让安迪飘走的故事情节。

00:35:29.389 --> 00:35:33.869
And I love that line where I say, did you say sandwich and white says sabotage.
我喜欢我说的那句话，你说三明治吗，白色说破坏。

00:35:33.869 --> 00:35:42.306
I remember Jen Salotta laughing her butt off and almost ruining a take because she cracked up every single time I said, did you say sandwich?
我记得珍·萨洛塔 (Jen Salotta) 笑得前仰后合，几乎毁掉了一次拍摄，因为每次我说“你是说三明治吗？”时她都会笑起来。

00:35:42.306 --> 00:35:47.033
But then I also just remember us hanging out in between scenes by our trailers.
但后来我也只记得我们在拖车旁的场景之间闲逛。

00:35:47.033 --> 00:35:53.196
We had like a little camp they set up and someone brought a football and we were throwing the football.
我们就像他们建立的一个小营地，有人带来了足球，我们就扔足球。

00:35:53.196 --> 00:36:02.590
And Harold Ramas came over in the morning and we would all have coffee together and sit outside one of the trailers having our coffee talking in the morning.
哈罗德·拉马斯早上过来，我们一起喝咖啡，坐在一辆拖车外面，早上喝咖啡聊天。

00:36:03.630 --> 00:36:09.458
It's just, it's amazing to me that I got to be a part of all of that.
只是，对我来说，我能成为这一切的一部分，真是太棒了。

00:36:09.458 --> 00:36:14.948
And I would say not to be totally sappy, but I am a bit of a sap.
我想说，不要完全傻瓜，但我确实有点傻瓜。

00:36:14.948 --> 00:36:27.449
One of the things that was really special to me about it was watching you as my best friend have this absolutely amazing monologue that had so much.
对我来说真正特别的事情之一就是看着你作为我最好的朋友进行这段绝对令人惊叹的独白，其中包含了很多内容。

00:36:27.449 --> 00:36:28.421
It was so long.
时间太长了。

00:36:28.421 --> 00:36:38.331
I remember when we got the script, it was like half a page and you nailed it in front of all of us and it had all this emotion and I was so proud of you.
我记得当我们拿到剧本时，它就像半页一样，你把它钉在我们所有人面前，它充满了所有的情感，我为你感到骄傲。

00:36:38.331 --> 00:36:42.800
Anyway, I don't know, I've just been very nostalgic for that episode.
无论如何，我不知道，我只是非常怀念那一集。

00:36:42.800 --> 00:36:44.354
What a wonderful memory.
多么美好的回忆啊。

00:36:44.354 --> 00:36:46.621
I really hold it close to my heart.
我真的把它放在心上。

00:36:46.621 --> 00:36:59.446
It's so funny that you picked that one, Angela, and for the reasons that you picked it, because there were two episodes that popped into my mind, and they're one right after the other in season two.
安吉拉，你选择了这一集真是太有趣了，而且你选择它的原因是因为有两集突然出现在我的脑海里，而且它们是第二季中的一集。

00:36:59.446 --> 00:37:01.519
And the first one is Booze Cruz.
第一个是 Booze Cruz。

00:37:01.519 --> 00:37:02.101
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:37:02.101 --> 00:37:11.364
Again, you'd be like, why are you picking the episode where we were up till the crack of dawn and we were all nauseous and you got lost at sea.
你又会想，为什么你要选择我们熬夜到黎明、我们都感到恶心而你在海上迷路的那一集。

00:37:11.364 --> 00:37:17.841
But you know, it's that thing where those memories are now part of the lore and the joy of the show.
但你知道，正是这些记忆现在成为了这部剧的传说和乐趣的一部分。

00:37:17.841 --> 00:37:20.172
They're part of the adventure of it.
他们是冒险的一部分。

00:37:20.172 --> 00:37:21.792
And we all really bonded.
我们真的很亲密。

00:37:21.792 --> 00:37:28.009
And that was the episode, Angela, where you guys found out you were going to be series regulars.
就在那一集，安吉拉，你们发现你们将成为该剧的常客。

00:37:29.210 --> 00:37:34.140
And so there was that extra added celebration and joy to that episode.
因此，这一集增添了额外的庆祝和欢乐。

00:37:34.140 --> 00:37:36.887
But then it was also just really funny.
但随后它也真的很有趣。

00:37:36.887 --> 00:37:39.141
It was fun being stuck together.
粘在一起很有趣。

00:37:39.141 --> 00:37:42.170
It was like a summer camp at sea, you know?
这就像海上夏令营，你知道吗？

00:37:43.530 --> 00:37:50.053
And we all got to stay in a hotel, even though we never saw each other, except on the boat, because we were all so tired.
我们都必须住在旅馆里，尽管除了在船上我们从未见过面，因为我们都太累了。

00:37:50.053 --> 00:37:53.449
And then, you know, the next episode after that was the injury.
然后，你知道，下一集就是受伤。

00:37:54.010 --> 00:38:02.270
And I remember this was when we were finally not worried we were going to be canceled every single week.
我记得那时我们终于不再担心每周都会被取消。

00:38:02.270 --> 00:38:05.527
And I think we could exhale a little bit.
我想我们可以松口气了。

00:38:05.527 --> 00:38:07.910
You guys were series regulars.
你们是系列常客。

00:38:07.910 --> 00:38:14.344
And then Mindy wrote this script that was just so bonkers and weird and so funny.
然后明迪写了这个剧本，真是疯狂、奇怪、有趣。

00:38:14.344 --> 00:38:23.319
And I laughed so hard shooting that episode with Steve and the butter and all of his antics with the bubble wrap.
拍摄史蒂夫和黄油以及他用泡沫包装纸做的所有滑稽动作的那一集时，我笑得很厉害。

00:38:23.320 --> 00:38:24.585
The bubble wrap.
气泡膜。

00:38:24.585 --> 00:38:25.085
Yeah.
是的。

00:38:25.085 --> 00:38:30.384
So that section right there, those are some of my fondest memories.
所以那部分是我最美好的回忆。

00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:30.780
Yeah.
是的。

00:38:30.780 --> 00:38:37.683
I mean, obviously I have favorite ones because I loved us all in the conference room, and we would get so punchy.
我的意思是，显然我有最喜欢的，因为我喜欢会议室里的我们所有人，而且我们会变得非常有力。

00:38:37.683 --> 00:38:47.274
So I look back on episodes where at the time, I was like, I cannot believe we're spending five days in this one room together, this one tiny conference room.
所以我回顾当时的情节，我当时想，我不敢相信我们在这一个房间，这一间小会议室里一起度过了五天。

00:38:47.079 --> 00:38:53.526
But those are the ones though that feel so special because we were all sort of in it together, you know?
但那些感觉很特别，因为我们都在一起，你知道吗？

00:38:53.526 --> 00:38:54.084
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

00:38:54.084 --> 00:39:00.593
I feel like if someone said, okay, I'm going to send you back in time and you get to reshoot one episode.
我觉得如果有人说，好吧，我会及时送你回去，你就可以重新拍摄一集。

00:39:00.593 --> 00:39:02.949
You get to re-experience shooting one.
您可以重新体验射击。

00:39:02.949 --> 00:39:06.792
I think I would choose the injury because it's in the bullpen.
我想我会选择伤病，因为它是在牛棚里。

00:39:06.792 --> 00:39:10.760
You know, I would want to go back in time and be in the bullpen.
你知道，我想回到过去，回到牛棚。

00:39:11.480 --> 00:39:11.980
Right.
正确的。

00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:15.845
And I just remember laughing so hard and it was so absurd.
我只记得我笑得很厉害，这太荒谬了。

00:39:15.845 --> 00:39:22.776
And we were all like still very young and fresh and we were experimenting and we were finding ourselves.
我们都还很年轻，很新鲜，我们在尝试，我们在寻找自己。

00:39:22.776 --> 00:39:26.042
And that's just such an exciting time creatively.
这真是一个令人兴奋的创造性时刻。

00:39:26.042 --> 00:39:27.975
That's such a great question.
这是一个很好的问题。

00:39:27.975 --> 00:39:37.572
If I could go back and relive one, I mean, that's really hard to pick because I loved dinner party, but I would want to redo one with everybody.
如果我可以回去重温一次，我的意思是，这真的很难选择，因为我喜欢晚宴，但我想和每个人重做一次。

00:39:37.572 --> 00:39:39.371
Yeah, in the office, right?
是的，在办公室，对吗？

00:39:39.371 --> 00:39:40.304
In the office.
在办公室里。

00:39:40.304 --> 00:39:45.369
And I was thinking, gosh, selfishly, I would also love women's appreciation.
我在想，天哪，自私地，我也喜欢女人的欣赏。

00:39:45.369 --> 00:39:51.167
Those scenes of us in that van and mayor of this van with all the trash and junk in it.
我们在那辆货车里的场景，以及这辆货车的市长，里面装满了垃圾和杂物。

00:39:51.167 --> 00:39:54.700
And you know, we got to spend a whole day with Steve.
你知道，我们必须和史蒂夫一起度过一整天。

00:39:54.599 --> 00:39:57.795
we got to have Steve to ourselves and that was so fun.
我们必须拥有史蒂夫一个人，这太有趣了。

00:39:57.795 --> 00:40:03.356
And of course, you know, we had scenes in the office too, so we would get to be with everyone.
当然，你知道，我们也有在办公室的场景，所以我们可以和每个人在一起。

00:40:03.356 --> 00:40:05.664
But I would do that day again for sure.
但我肯定会再次这样做。

00:40:05.664 --> 00:40:06.164
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:06.880 --> 00:40:07.380
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:07.380 --> 00:40:08.698
Well, thanks, Katherine.
嗯，谢谢，凯瑟琳。

00:40:08.698 --> 00:40:13.366
Thanks for letting us answer that question that we've asked so many people ourselves.
感谢您让我们回答这个我们自己问过很多人的问题。

00:40:13.366 --> 00:40:14.684
It's fun to think about.
想想就很有趣。

00:40:14.684 --> 00:40:15.184
Yeah.
是的。

00:40:15.184 --> 00:40:17.490
And thank you guys so much for writing in.
非常感谢你们的来信。

00:40:17.039 --> 00:40:20.159
We're really just loving doing these segments with you all.
我们真的很喜欢和你们一起做这些部分。

00:40:20.159 --> 00:40:21.533
So go to officeladies.com.
因此，请访问officeladies.com。

00:40:21.533 --> 00:40:23.383
You can click on submit a question.
您可以点击提交问题。

00:40:23.383 --> 00:40:26.079
We have lots of fun folders where you can write in.
我们有很多有趣的文件夹，您可以在其中写入内容。

00:40:26.800 --> 00:40:29.421
Yeah, we've gotten really organized, everybody.
是的，大家，我们已经组织得很好了。

00:40:29.421 --> 00:40:29.978
We did it.
我们做到了。

00:40:29.978 --> 00:40:33.324
We're very grateful to Iliana who helps us with our website.
我们非常感谢 Iliana 为我们的网站提供的帮助。

00:40:33.324 --> 00:40:40.239
We have a special folder for second drinks where we want you to go in there and tell us your favorite moments from episodes.
我们有一个专门的文件夹用于存放第二杯饮料，我们希望您能进去并告诉我们您在剧集中最喜欢的时刻。

00:40:40.239 --> 00:40:47.991
And then we also have a folder for around the town for chit chat questions and now officially a folder for the office question of the week.
然后我们还有一个文件夹用于存放城镇周围的闲聊问题，现在正式一个文件夹用于存放本周的办公室问题。

00:40:47.991 --> 00:40:49.385
Yeah, so go check it out.
是啊，所以去看看吧。

00:40:49.385 --> 00:40:51.616
And we hope you guys have the best week.
我们希望你们度过了最美好的一周。

00:40:51.616 --> 00:40:53.289
We appreciate you all so much.
我们非常感谢你们大家。

00:40:53.289 --> 00:40:57.360
And a big thank you to Craig Thomas and Josh Radner for joining us today.
非常感谢克雷格·托马斯和乔什·拉德纳今天加入我们。

00:40:57.360 --> 00:41:00.041
We'll see you next week everyone.
大家下周见。

00:41:00.041 --> 00:41:01.098
See you then.
到时候见。

00:41:01.098 --> 00:41:04.429
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢您收听《办公室女士》。

00:41:04.429 --> 00:41:09.710
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》是《奥德赛》的演示，由珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金赛制作。

00:41:09.710 --> 00:41:13.917
Our senior producer is Matt Beagle and our audio engineer is Sam Keefer.
我们的高级制作人是 Matt Beagle，我们的音频工程师是 Sam Keefer。

00:41:13.917 --> 00:41:16.839
Odyssey's executive producer is Leah Reese Dennis.
奥德赛的执行制片人是利亚·里斯·丹尼斯。

00:41:16.839 --> 00:41:19.877
Office Ladies was mixed and mastered by Bill Schulz.
《Office Ladies》由比尔·舒尔茨 (Bill Schulz) 混音并掌握。

00:41:19.877 --> 00:41:23.150
Our theme The same song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题同一首歌是克里德·布拉顿（Creed Bratton）的《橡胶树》（Rubber Tree）。

